  "about": "\n                <p>\n                    Neilson Koerner-Safrata is a video game designer and software developer. Known for his work in interaction design.\n                </p>\n                \n                <p>\n                    He lives in San Francisco, works at the spatial intelligence company <a href=\"https://worldlabs.ai/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">World Labs</a>, and maintains the <a href=\"https://oakwood-studio.github.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Oakwood St.</a> studio.\n                </p>\n                \n                <p>\n                    As the first designer at <a href=\"https://tenderclaws.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tender Claws</a>, Neilson developed the games Virtual Virtual Reality and Tendar, combining emerging tech with theatrical arts and game design. Afterwards, he co-founded <a href=\"https://scrnprnt.ca/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SCRNPRNT</a> with his twin brother <a href=\"https://milanks.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Milan</a>. Their video games included an online chatroom for the animal civilizations of Age of Empires II, a memorial to the last Counter-Strike server, and an interactive listening experience with musician Sam Tudor. \n                    \n                </p>\n                \n                <p>\n                    He then moved to the Bay Area, creating animation systems for an interactive talking dog driven by realtime language models.\n                </p>\n                \n                <p>\n                    In the past, Neilson has contributed to The Terraforming design program, researching the connection between space travel and death, and has been active in the communities of ZSpace, DWeb, Trust, Autonomous Worlds, South Park Commons, and Stochastic Labs.\n                </p>\n\n            ",
